@startuml checkin_gate
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' checkin_gate — v28.2 part 1: WHEN the morning check-in knocks. Pure.
' The §A spine's third application: the model will HOLD the conversation
' (part 2), but whether to knock is code — deterministic and stingy.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The check-in gate — once, in the morning, only when the day is heavy

start
:a sweep asks checkin::shouldOffer(data, now, lastOffered);

if (06:00 ≤ now < 11:00?) then (no)
  :silence — a morning check-in at
  15:40 is a different, worse feature;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (already offered today?\nlastOffered == today) then (yes)
  :silence — once means once,
  asking twice is nagging squared;
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (isDayHeavy?\n≥5h planned  OR\n≥2 tasks due within 2 days) then (no)
  :silence — a quiet Tuesday does
  not need a wellness interview
  (§G.1, verbatim);
  stop
else (yes)
  :OFFER — part 2 turns this into a
  toast whose action opens the chat
  with the check-in waiting;
  note right
    Mood, once answered, is the first
    stored fact the app cannot derive:
    data.json, format v12, one per day,
    trimmed at 14 by the midnight knock.
    The NOTE never enters a briefing —
    pinned by test, not by comment.
  end note
  stop
endif
@enduml
